<title>GERMANY: Haindl Finance says plans mark Eurobond issue soon.</title>
<headline>Haindl Finance says plans mark Eurobond issue soon.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Haindl Finance BV of the Netherlands said on Thursday it planned to issue a syndicated mark Eurobond in the next few weeks with a maturity of seven to 10 years in a volume of between 200 and 300 million marks.</p>
<p>The issue will be guaranteed by Haindl Papier GmbH, of Germany, and the joint lead managers will be Bayerische Vereinsbank and Deutsche Morgan Grenfell, Haindl said in a statement.</p>
<p>It said it expected the issue to be listed on exchanges in Frankfurt and Munich.</p>
<p>-- Kate Kelland, Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
